---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { site, shortDate } from '../data/site';

const updated = '2026-11-13';
const link = 'accent-text underline underline-offset-4 hover:no-underline';
---
<Base title={`Privacy · ${site.name}`} description="What raymond.sg collects: usage statistics through Google Analytics, and nothing else unless you email me.">
  <Header />
  <main id="main" class="max-w-[1360px] mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6 lg:px-12">
    <article class="max-w-2xl py-14 sm:py-20 lg:py-24">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-2">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-medium tracking-tight mb-4">What happens to your data here</h1>
      <p class="text-sm muted mb-12">Last updated {shortDate(updated)}</p>

      <div class="space-y-10 leading-relaxed [&_h2]:text-lg [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:tracking-tight [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_p]:muted [&_p+p]:mt-3">
        <section>
          <p>This site has no accounts, forms or ads, and it doesn't ask for your name or contact details. The only data it gathers is usage statistics, which don't tell me who you are.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Analytics</h2>
          <p>I use Google Analytics 4 to see how many people visit and which pages and links they use. It sets cookies to tell new visits from repeat ones, and records things like the pages you view, the site that sent you, your approximate location, your device and browser, and clicks on project links, downloads and my email address. Google keeps this data for 14 months, and may process it outside Singapore.</p>
          <p>The site works the same without it. To opt out, block cookies in your browser or install <a class={link} href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google's opt-out add-on</a>. More on <a class={link} href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses this data</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Hosting</h2>
          <p>The site is hosted on Cloudflare, which processes your IP address to deliver pages and protect the site from attacks.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Email</h2>
          <p>If you email <a class={link} href={`mailto:${site.email}`} data-track="contact" data-project="privacy_email">{site.email}</a>, I use your message only to reply, and I'll delete it if you ask. The same address works for any question about this page.</p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-14"><a class="arrow-link" href="/">Back to home</a></p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>
